cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its failure analysis in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "PINN vs Split-Step Fourier for the 1D Schrödinger/Gross-Pitaevskii Equation: An Honest Benchmark"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Nidhal"
    given-names: "Zitouni"
    alias: "NodeBox-Labs"
    affiliation: "NodeBox Labs"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000" # Update if you have one
repository-code: "https://github.com/NodeBox-Labs/pinn-vs-ssf-schrodinger"
url: "https://github.com/NodeBox-Labs/pinn-vs-ssf-schrodinger"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, reproducible benchmark comparing Physics-Informed Neural Networks (PINNs)
  against a Strang split-step Fourier reference solver for the 1D Gross-Pitaevskii and
  Schrödinger equations. The study rigorously documents PINN failure modes (spectral bias,
  phase accumulation) on solitons and long-time dynamics, providing a controlled baseline
  for future scientific-ML research.
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - pinn
  - schrodinger equation
  - gross-pitaevskii equation
  - split-step fourier
  - deep learning
  - scientific machine learning
  - spectral bias
